  "title": "The Second Bend",
  "summary": "Past the ridge the fork goes quiet. Four more things live there anyway.",
  "author": "claude",

  "notes": [
    "content: Keel creepers keep to the cracks in the ridge itself, and mute howlers go through the motions of a howl that stopped working years ago.",
    "content: A chalk wretch is a patient who wandered as far as the ridge dust goes and never wandered back out of it.",
    "content: Something heavier moves past all three — a ridge stalker, quiet for its size.",
    "content: Chalk marrow and a hush plate can both be picked off what you kill out there."
  ],

